nrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}}]},{"fancy_title":"Grokbot failed to connect to computer","id":170474,"title":"Grokbot failed to connect to computer","slug":"grokbot-failed-to-connect-to-computer","posts_count":1,"reply_count":0,"highest_post_number":1,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T14:47:43.053Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-03T14:47:43.118Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-03T14:47:43.118Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nGrok Bot \nDescribe the Bug\nNew Grok Bot installation, v0.36.0, macOS. Setup fails with “Can’t reach your computer”. Tested normal Wi-Fi and iPhone hotspot on a separate mobile\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":31,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":"latest single","description":"Original Poster, Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":135966,"username":"ALIN_FARAH","name":"ALIN FARAH","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/ecd19e/{size}.png","trust_level":0}}]},{"fancy_title":"Grok Bot Windows - can\u0026rsquo;t reach computer","id":170462,"title":"Grok Bot Windows - can't reach computer","slug":"grok-bot-windows-cant-reach-computer","posts_count":4,"reply_count":1,"highest_post_number":7,"image_url":null,"created_at":"2026-09-03T13:21:00.706Z","last_posted_at":"2026-09-03T15:01:48.713Z","bumped":true,"bumped_at":"2026-09-03T15:01:48.713Z","archetype":"regular","unseen":false,"pinned":false,"unpinned":null,"excerpt":"Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nGrok Bot \nDescribe the Bug\nGrok Bot on Windows. \nError: Can’t reach Grok Bot’s computer. \nNo VPN, no Zscaler. \nDNS set to 1.1.1.1 and 8.8.8.8. \nPhone hotspot also failed. \nRet\u0026hellip;","visible":true,"closed":false,"archived":false,"bookmarked":null,"liked":null,"thumbnails":null,"tags":[{"id":416,"name":"grok-bot","slug":"grok-bot"},{"id":408,"name":"networking","slug":"networking"}],"tags_descriptions":{},"like_count":0,"views":97,"category_id":6,"featured_link":null,"op_like_count":0,"has_accepted_answer":false,"posters":[{"extras":null,"description":"Original Poster","user":{"id":135910,"username":"Amy_Ostler","name":"Amy Ostler","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/b5ac83/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":null,"description":"Recent Poster","user":{"id":135960,"username":"Goten","name":"Goten","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/g/ecb155/{size}.png","trust_level":0}},{"extras":"latest","description":"Most Recent Poster","user":{"id":750,"username":"deanrie","name":"Dean Rie","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/deanrie/{size}/1263_2.png","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":4}}]}],"summarizable":false,"has_cached_summary":false,"valid_reactions":["heart","+1","crossed_fingers","clap","laughing","open_mouth","confetti_ball","hugs","heavy_plus_sign","heart_eyes","sunglasses","cursor"],"accepted_answers":[{"id":483252,"name":"Colin","username":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-04T12:42:19.519Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/andyfraussen\"\u003e@andyfraussen\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report, and sorry for the trouble.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGood news first: your computer and your bots are fine. They are still running on our side, and a couple of routines even completed this morning. The apps just cannot reach them because they are no longer signed in.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom our side it looks like the sessions on your account were revoked from the Active Sessions list on \u003ca href=\"http://cursor.com\"\u003ecursor.com\u003c/a\u003e this morning (around 07:25 UTC). Revoking sessions signs out every device, including the Grok Bot desktop app and the iOS app. Those apps are still holding on to the old sign-in, and instead of asking you to sign in again they show it as a connection problem. That is also why Retry, Update and Reset do nothing, and why VPN or mobile data made no difference. The 0.39.0 update landed after this had already started and is not the cause.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo fix it, sign out and back in on each device:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn Grok Bot on your Mac, click your name / avatar at the bottom left of the sidebar.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChoose Sign out and confirm.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSign in again with the same account (Sign in with Grok, andy@fraussen.dev).\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWait a minute after signing in. Your bots should load.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn your iPhone, open Grok Bot, go to Settings, sign out, then sign back in with the same account.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you cannot find a Sign out option on the Mac, quit Grok Bot completely (right-click its Dock icon and choose Quit), reopen it and try again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnabling Privacy Mode was not needed for this and did not cause it, so set it however you prefer. Let me know if either device still does not connect after signing back in!\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"topic_id":170568,"url":"/t/cant-access-grok-bot-anymore-probably-after-updating-to-0-39-0/170568/5","accepter_name":"Andy","accepter_username":"andyfraussen"}],"has_accepted_answer":true,"can_create_shared_issue":false,"shared_issue_visible":false,"can_vote":false,"vote_count":0,"user_voted":false,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_id":null,"discourse_zendesk_plugin_zendesk_url":"https://your-url.zendesk.com/agent/tickets/","details":{"can_edit":false,"notification_level":1,"participants":[{"id":136115,"username":"andyfraussen","name":"Andy","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/f07891/{size}.png","post_count":2,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"trust_level":0},{"id":87436,"username":"Colin","name":"Colin","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/colin/{size}/90452_2.png","post_count":1,"primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_color":"","flair_bg_color":"","flair_group_id":42,"admin":true,"moderator":true,"trust_level":3},{"id":136184,"username":"Liam_Serour","name":"Liam Serour","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/898d66/{size}.png","post_count":1,"primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"trust_level":0}],"created_by":{"id":136115,"username":"andyfraussen","name":"Andy","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/a/f07891/{size}.png"},"last_poster":{"id":136184,"username":"Liam_Serour","name":"Liam Serour","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/l/898d66/{size}.png"}},"bookmarks":[]}